# Copy to .env.local and fill in only if you want AI-generated roasts.
# Everything works without this file — 20 built-in roasts are used instead.

# ⚠️  READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A KEY
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the JavaScript bundle. In a purely
# client-side app that means ANYONE WHO OPENS THE PAGE CAN READ YOUR API KEY.
# That is fine for a tool you run locally on your own machine. It is NOT fine
# for anything you deploy publicly — use VITE_ROAST_PROXY_URL below instead.

# --- Recommended for anything deployed --------------------------------------
# Your own endpoint that holds the key server-side and returns {"roast": "..."}.
# Takes priority over the direct keys below. No secret reaches the browser.
# VITE_ROAST_PROXY_URL=https://your-worker.example.com/roast

# --- Local use only ----------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Default model is claude-haiku-4-5: a roast has to land while you are still
# slouching, so latency matters more than eloquence here. Swap in a larger model
# if you want wittier lines and can accept the extra second.
# VITE_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# VITE_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
